      },
      "message": "fix(circular): rings post as arcs, not 512 fixed chords\n\nA Circular ring was a closed 512-chord polygon at every radius, and the\nhelix entry's stand-down ramp walked it: one 6 mm hole was 74,131 moves\nof 0.006 mm. Each ring-level is now two half-turn arcs about the\nauthored centre (G3 climb / G2 conventional, the old travel and start\npoint); the planning polygon's chord count comes from ARC_FIT_TOL (a\npower of two dividing the 512-gon certificate), and the zig-zag ramp on\na ring flies helical arcs on the ring (same legs, length and angle).\nThe repro is 417 moves; verify verdicts are unchanged.\n\nFixes #1558\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
