        "date": "2026-11-14T01:11:50Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(circular): ring ramp proves its ring; no sub-resolution arcs\n\nReview fixes for PR #1601 (M3, on f3cb9d2):\n\n- push_zig_ring moves to crates/motion/src/ring_zig.rs and flies arcs\n  only when the planned prefix lies on the ring (vertices within\n  ON_RING_TOL, the last point inside by at most ARC_FIT_TOL), its first\n  step turns in the arcs' sense, and the leg's arc end lands on the\n  prefix end. Anything else posts push_zig's chords, whatever the\n  ring_zig flag says.\n- MIN_ARC_CHORD (0.01 mm): a ramp piece or a ring half turn whose chord\n  is under it posts straight, so no posted arc can round its ends\n  together (4-decimal inch) and read as a full circle.\n- Pins: the ramp law on every helical piece (slope along the flown arc,\n  equal legs, travel = drop / tan), a non-circular prefix and a flipped\n  sense stay chords, sub-resolution ramps and rings stay straight in mm\n  and inch, ring_zig off by default; a circular_ring_arcs CL golden of\n  the issue's repro (417 moves).\n\nRefs #1558\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
